## Required workflow
1. Read `.agents/skills/xenoblade-decomp/SKILL.md` and PLAN.md §§2, 3, 17.
2. Always use `.venv/bin/python3`.
3. For each target, smallest size first, then highest instruction_match:
   - `python3 tools/coop/run.py targets show <id>`
   - `python3 tools/coop/run.py targets claim <id> --owner midband-01`
   - Search KB: `python3 tools/mwcc_kb.py search "<symbol>" --kind reference --json` then mismatch terms.
   - Iterate with `python3 tools/coop/hexdiff.py <unit> --symbol <mangled> --brief` (not raw ninja). Revert if mismatch counts rise.
   - After hexdiff is clean (0 mismatches): `python3 tools/coop/run.py cycle <id> --hypothesis "..." --next-change "..."`
   - Release the claim. Append `docs/evidence/decomp/attempts.jsonl`. Breakthroughs go to MWCC_PATTERNS.md (general) or MWCC_CASES.md (per-target).
4. After 3 non-improving attempts: record an open-item packet (status/%, size, categories, ruled-out, exact residual, next 3 experiments) and move on.
5. Hard rules: no `--smt`/`--linked`/plain `run.py diff`; no asm/register/stack tricks outside PLAN §17.6; no git push; no commit unless asked; do not edit units outside your list; do not demote 0% FULL_MATCH rows (different problem).

